{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The large ring is not selectable; selecting its center leaves the first small ring active. So level 4 reuses the level-3 physical affordance: a small ring must push the large one. The two small rings are selectable and move three pixels per arrow. I’m using a bounded state search keyed by the visible frame plus the active small-ring position, prioritized by minimum assignment distance to the three target centers; this preserves hidden selection state without inspecting runtime internals."}}
